Attacks on Switches:
1.CDP Information Disclosure:
CDP (Cisco Discovery Protocol) is a protocol used between swithces or routers to borrow configuration from another similar device, the attacker could use it to disclose information about these devices in the network.

2.MAC Flooding:
flooding a switch with so many new mac addresses which will either enforce it either to shutdown or to act like a hub.

3.DHCP Manupliation:
the attacker will try to listen to any dhcp request and then respond back with a fake default gateway ip (i.e the attacker ip) quickly before the dhcp server to acheive MitM

4.STP Manupilation:
the stp protocol is used mainly between swtiches to prevent loops while forwarding the traffic, the attacker can exploit this to perform a DoS attack.

5.VLAN Hopping:
in this type of attack the attacker will compromise the switch to give himself the ability to jump from one vlan to the other.


