801 1.X:
is standard for port-based network access control that will allow a router or a switch (with the help of an authentication server) to authenticate whoever tries to plug in an ethernet cable or tryies to connect wirelessly.

the device that is trying to gain access to the network should have a supplicant client that will send an access request to the authenticator (Switch), the authenticator will pass the request to a backend authentication server which in turn will say if that device has access or not.

